-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: Infernal Bargain retimed to 1 shard per second for 4 sec
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- woa_2026_08_02_00.sql set the channel to DurationIndex 27 with a 1500 ms
-- tick.  Its comments claimed "6 second channel -> exactly 4 ticks", but
-- index 27 is 3000 ms, so the channel only ever landed 2 ticks and the
-- 4-stack buff could never be filled from a single cast.
--
-- Retimed for all three ranks (63349 / 63350 / 63351):
--   DurationIndex    27 (3000 ms) -> 35 (4000 ms)
--   EffectAmplitude1 1500 -> 1000
-- -> ticks at 1/2/3/4 sec, 4 shards, 4 stacks, as the design intended.
--
-- The tooltip's "every 1.5 sec" is updated to "every 1 sec"; the duration
-- reads from $d, so it follows the new DurationIndex on its own.  Nothing
-- else changes -- the damage reduction on effect 2, the per-rank buff in
-- EffectTriggerSpell1, and the C++ (spell_warl_infernal_bargain) are all
-- tick-count agnostic.
-- ===========================================================================


